# vesma-mcp-front platform env slot — template.
#
# Copy to the env.d slot of the target plane, make it 0600:
#
#   user:   cp mcp-front.env.example ~/.vesma/env.d/mcp-front.env
#           chmod 600 ~/.vesma/env.d/mcp-front.env
#   system: sudo cp mcp-front.env.example /etc/vesma/env.d/mcp-front.env
#           sudo chmod 600 /etc/vesma/env.d/mcp-front.env
#           sudo chown root:vesma /etc/vesma/env.d/mcp-front.env   # if root-installed
#
# Fail-closed: the supervisor refuses the front start unless this file
# exists with EXACTLY mode 0600, owned by the supervisor user, and
# OUTSIDE the manifests directory (layout §3.5, LY-03).
#
# THE FRONT STORES NO SECRETS (ADR-0050 C2): harness Authorization
# headers pass through UNREAD to the core — this component validates no
# tokens and holds no credentials, so there is nothing secret to put
# here, ever. The 0600 ritual stays because the env.d slot is the
# component's fail-closed config channel (and where future front knobs
# land). Never commit a filled copy of this file.
#
# The core MCP plane this front forwards to (loopback only — the module
# refuses any non-loopback target, because this URL is where harness
# tokens GO; C2). Default instance core = 127.0.0.1:8787, plane = /mcp/.
VESMA_FRONT_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8787/mcp/
